@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-repeals`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-construction`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-application`

-- Expectations that are MEANT TO FAIL: seven readings that the text of the Interpretation Act 1978 rules out, each written as a
-- test. Each is a plausible misreading, and each is stated here as an assertion so that the run shows the encoding does not
-- produce it. check.sh expects exactly 7 failed assertions in this file and no other error; encoding.json names the file under
-- `expected_red`. If one of these starts to pass, the module has changed what the text says, and that is a finding.

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of enactment`
      d    IS A DATE
      provision IS A `Provision on coming into force`
GIVETH AN `An enactment`
`an enactment` kind d provision MEANS `An enactment` WITH
    `its kind`                             IS kind
    `the day it was passed or made`        IS d
    `what it says about coming into force` IS provision

GIVEN e IS AN `An enactment`
GIVETH A DATE
`the day on which it comes into force` e MEANS (`section 4 — when the enactment comes into force` e)'s `the day`

-- 1. "An Act that says nothing comes into force on the day after the Royal Assent." The text: s 4(b), "at the beginning of the day on
--    which the Act receives the Royal Assent". The day is 10 March 2026, not the 11th.
#ASSERT `the day on which it comes into force` (`an enactment` `an Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) `no provision`) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 11)

-- 2. "An Act whose day is to be fixed later binds from its passing until the day is fixed." The text: s 4(a), provision made for a
--    particular day, "at the beginning of that day"; the day is 1 June 2026.
#ASSERT `the day on which it comes into force` (`an enactment` `an Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) (`a day to be fixed later` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)))) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 10)

-- 3. "Subordinate legislation that says nothing is governed by s 4(b) like an Act." The text: s 23(1) excepts s 4(b).
#ASSERT `section 4(b) applies to` (`an enactment` `subordinate legislation` (YMD 2026 3 10) `no provision`)

-- 4. "The repealed enactment remains in force through the day on which the substituted provisions come into force." The text: s 17(1),
--    "until the substituted provisions come into force", and s 4(a) brings them into force at the beginning of that day.
#ASSERT `section 17(1) provides that the repealed enactment remains in force on` TRUE (`an enactment` `an Act` (YMD 2026 3 10) (`a particular day` (YMD 2026 6 1))) (YMD 2026 6 1)

-- 5. "A range 'from section 5 to section 8' leaves out the sections it names." The text: s 20(1), "the portion described or cited
--    includes the words, sections or other parts referred to".
#ASSERT NOT `section 20(1) provides that the portion described or cited includes` 5 8 5 FALSE

-- 6. "An instrument may come into force at the beginning of the day on which its parent Act is passed." The text: s 13, "at any time
--    after the passing of the Act"; the beginning of the day is before the passing.
#ASSERT `section 13 permits an instrument made under the Act to come into force at` (`An anticipatory power` WITH `the day the Act was passed` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the Act or provision does not come into force immediately on its passing` IS TRUE, `the power is to make subordinate legislation, make appointments, give notices, prescribe forms or do any other thing for the purposes of the Act` IS TRUE, `it is necessary or expedient for bringing the Act or a provision into force, or for giving full effect to it at or after the time it comes into force` IS TRUE, `the contrary intention appears` IS FALSE) (`Coming into force` WITH `the day` IS YMD 2026 3 10, `the moment within the day` IS `the beginning of the day`)

-- 7. "Section 14 reaches every Act passed after 1889 in whole." The text: Sch 2 para 3, "Section 14 so far as it relates to rules,
--    regulations or byelaws".
#ASSERT `the extent to which the provision applies to an Act passed on` `section 14` (YMD 1950 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
